TITLE:: Paint
summary:: The painting register of Synesthesia — colours and tools over the audio words
categories:: Live Coding>Synesthesia
related:: Guides/Synesthesia, Reference/Synesthesia-Reference, Classes/Synesthesia, Classes/Symbol, Classes/Pattern, Classes/NodeProxy, Classes/Broadcast

DESCRIPTION::
The painting register describes timbre the way it is perceived — as colour — and
application in time the way a painter would: strong::pigment × applicator::. It
sits over the engineering words of link::Guides/Synesthesia:: and never replaces
them. Every colour word evaluates to the same plain objects as every other word (a
link::Classes/Pbind::, a link::Classes/NodeProxy::), so you can drop the register
at any moment and reach the descriptive layer underneath: a stroke is a Pbind with
code::\hue::, code::\sat:: and code::\val:: keys, a move is a link::Classes/Pbindf::
on one of them.

subsection:: Colours

A colour is a coordinate in the space every voice of the palette speaks —
code::hue::, code::sat::, code::val::, each 0..1 (the contract in the companion
repo's code::CONVENTIONS.md::): emphasis::hue:: is an angle on the voice's timbre
wheel (0 and 1 are the same place), emphasis::sat:: is hue-identity strength (0 is
grey, 1 vivid, the extreme top neon), emphasis::val:: is light (0 is black, 1 is
air). A colour also has a emphasis::spread::: pigment is never flat, so each event
draws its own coordinates from a small neighbourhood of the tube.

The palette is eleven tubes named after the screen colour wheel — code::red
orange yellow green cyan blue violet magenta grey white black:: — because a
colour's timbre coordinates emphasis::are:: its screen colour: link::Classes/Broadcast::
sends them with every painted event, and a VJ can draw them unchanged. The names
are a first set to play and rename by ear; the lexicon is discovered, not
specified. Add your own tubes in your setup file:
code::Paint.palette[\rust] = Paint.color(0.05, 0.8, 0.35);::

Wherever a colour is expected you may give a palette name (code::\orange::), an
array code::[hue, sat, val, spread]::, an event code::(hue: 0.3, sat: 0.7, val: 0.5)::,
a link::Classes/Color::, or a mix of two colours (link::#*mix::).

subsection:: Tools

A tool is one voice and one way of applying it in time. The voices are the
SynthDefs of the companion repo's code::Setup/SynthDefs:: (loaded by
code::Setup.scd::); link::#*tools:: maps each tool to its voice, and any SynthDef
that speaks code::hue::/code::sat::/code::val:: can take a tool's place. Pitch and
time stay music words: chord names, scale degrees, step strings and durations ride
in the tool call unchanged, and placement (code::at::, a pan position) belongs to
the stroke, not the pigment. The words live on link::Classes/Symbol::, so
code::\orange.brush("Cm7 G7"):: and code::brush(\orange, "Cm7 G7"):: are the same
expression.

table::
## strong::Word:: || strong::Voice:: || strong::Application in time::
## code::\c.brush(notes, dur):: || code::\brush:: || a sustained, legato stroke — chord names, degrees or a step string
## code::\c.mark(notes, dur):: || code::\mark:: || discrete pitched events
## code::\c.dab(steps, step):: || code::\mark:: || rhythmic touches on one note; a touch per bar by default
## code::\c.drip(rate, notes):: || code::\mark:: || sparse stochastic touches: Dust-like timing, notes drawn at random
## code::\c.spray(root, dens):: || code::\spray:: (code::\sprayb:: over a buffer) || a grain cloud at the root
## code::\c.wash(root):: || code::\wash:: || a texture bed at the root
::

Every stroke is tagged for Broadcast with code::\syn_brush:: (the tool),
code::\syn_material:: (the voice) and code::\syn_color:: (the tube), and goes out
under code::/syn/paint/<tool>/:: as amp, pitch, notes, size, dur, hue, sat, val and count, one value per address (link::Classes/Broadcast::).

subsection:: Moves

Perceptual sculpt verbs — code::.darker::, code::.lighter::, code::.paler::,
code::.saturate::, code::.warmer::, code::.cooler::, each taking a step size, and
code::.paint(colour):: to recolour outright. On a link::Classes/Pattern:: they
return a new pattern that steps the axis from the value each event already carries
(or the voice's own default), so moves chain and compound. On a
link::Classes/NodeProxy:: they act on what the proxy holds: a pattern source is
reassigned (crossfaded, on the grid), a synth source has its code::hue::/code::sat::/
code::val:: controls moved — so a drone recipe joins the register the moment it
names those controls. Warmer and cooler step toward the warm and cool poles of
the wheel the shorter way round, never past them.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: palette
The tubes: an link::Classes/IdentityDictionary:: from name to colour. Edit it in
your setup file to add, rename or retune a tube.

METHOD:: colors
The tube names, sorted.

METHOD:: color
A colour. With numbers, a new one; with anything else, the colour that thing
denotes.
argument:: hue
a number (the hue, 0..1, wrapping), or a colour form: a palette name as Symbol or
String, code::[hue, sat, val, spread]::, an event with code::hue::/code::sat::/
code::val::/code::spread:: keys, or a link::Classes/Color::.
argument:: sat
0..1 (default 0.6). Only with a numeric hue.
argument:: val
0..1 (default 0.5). Only with a numeric hue.
argument:: spread
how far each event may wander from the tube: hue ± spread, sat and val ± spread/2
(default 0.03).
argument:: name
an optional name, used as the code::\syn_color:: tag.
returns:: an link::Classes/Event:: with the keys code::hue::, code::sat::, code::val::,
code::spread::, code::name::. An unknown palette name, or something that is not a
colour, is an error naming it.

METHOD:: mix
A pigment between two colours: sat, val and spread interpolate; hue takes the
shorter way round the wheel, so red and magenta mix through the purples.
argument:: a
a colour (any form).
argument:: b
a colour (any form).
argument:: x
0 is strong::a::, 1 is strong::b:: (default 0.5).
returns:: a colour, named after both tubes when both are named (code::\orange_blue::).

METHOD:: colorKeys
The link::Classes/Pbind:: pairs that paint a stroke: code::\hue::, code::\sat::
and code::\val:: as per-event samples within the colour's spread, and the
code::\syn_color:: tag.
argument:: color
a colour (any form).
returns:: an array of key/pattern pairs — code::Pbind(*Paint.colorKeys(\blue))::.

METHOD:: tools
The map from tool to voice: an link::Classes/IdentityDictionary::. Rebind a tool
to any SynthDef that speaks the colour axes: code::Paint.tools[\dab] = \kick::.

METHOD:: brush
METHOD:: mark
METHOD:: dab
METHOD:: drip
METHOD:: spray
METHOD:: wash
The tool words with the colour first — the bodies behind the words on
link::Classes/Symbol#-brush#Symbol:: (a tube's name) and on link::Classes/Event::
(any other colour: a mix, or code::(hue: sat: val:):: written out), which forward
here. Arguments as documented on Symbol, after strong::color::.
argument:: color
a colour (any form link::#*color:: accepts).
returns:: a link::Classes/Pbind::
discussion::
code::
Paint.brush(\orange, "Cm7 G7");             // the same stroke three ways
\orange.brush("Cm7 G7");
brush(\orange, "Cm7 G7");
\orange.mix(\blue, 0.3).brush("Cm7 G7");    // a mix takes the words too
(hue: 0.3, sat: 0.7, val: 0.5).mark("0 3 5");
::

METHOD:: voiceFor
The voice a tool owns; an unknown tool is an error.

METHOD:: stroke
The Pbind every tool word returns: the tool's voice, the given pairs, the
placement, the pigment and the Broadcast tags.
argument:: tool
a key of link::#*tools::.
argument:: color
a colour (any form).
argument:: pairs
the tool's own key/value pairs (pitch, time, density…).
argument:: at
pan position, −1..1 or a pattern (default 0).
returns:: a link::Classes/Pbind::

METHOD:: strokeKind
What a notes argument is.
returns:: code::\chords:: (chord names such as code::"Cm7 G7"::, or an array of
Symbols), code::\steps:: (a step string such as code::"x..X"::), or code::\degs::
(scale degrees — a string or an array of numbers).

METHOD:: notePairs
The pitch/time pairs of a pitched stroke, from any notes form.
argument:: notes
chord names, a step string, or degrees (see link::#*strokeKind::).
argument:: dur
beats per note, or per character of a step string (default 0.5). May be a pattern
(not with a step string).
argument:: amp
amplitude (default 0.3). Accents in a step string multiply it.
argument:: oct
the octave (default 5).
argument:: shuffle
true draws notes at random instead of in order (default false).
returns:: an array of key/pattern pairs.

METHOD:: rootPattern
The root a cloud sits on, as something a code::\freq:: key can hold.
argument:: root
a number, a link::Classes/Pattern::, a control proxy (followed live, through
code::Pkr::), a function, or nil — then the canvas's code::~r:: if it has a
source, otherwise 55 Hz.

METHOD:: bufferOf
The buffer a buffer cloud sprays: a link::Classes/Buffer::, or the name of a folder
in code::d:: (its latest capture — what code::rec:: appended last).

METHOD:: moved
One step of a move, pure.
argument:: value
the current value of the axis.
argument:: axis
code::\hue::, code::\sat:: or code::\val::.
argument:: delta
the step. sat and val clip to 0..1; hue wraps.
argument:: toward
for hue only: a pole to step toward the shorter way round, never past it. Without
one, hue simply adds and wraps.
returns:: the new value.

METHOD:: move
A move on a pattern: a link::Classes/Pbindf:: that steps the axis from the value
each event carries, or from the voice's default (link::#*axisDefault::) when the
pattern never set it.
argument:: pattern
an event pattern.
argument:: axis
code::\hue::, code::\sat:: or code::\val::.
argument:: delta
the step.
argument:: toward
a hue pole, or nil.
returns:: a new pattern.

METHOD:: verbMove
The table the verbs share: the axis, delta and pole for a verb name
(code::\darker::, code::\lighter::, code::\paler::, code::\saturate::,
code::\warmer::, code::\cooler::) and a step size.
returns:: code::[axis, delta]:: or code::[axis, delta, pole]::.

METHOD:: axisDefault
A voice's own natural value for an axis, read from its link::Classes/SynthDesc::;
the contract's defaults (hue 0.05, sat 0.6, val 0.5) when the voice is unknown.

METHOD:: warmPole
METHOD:: coolPole
The hue positions code::.warmer:: and code::.cooler:: move toward: orange
(0.08) and blue (0.62).

EXAMPLES::

code::
// after Setup.scd (the voices live in the companion repo's Setup/SynthDefs)
Paint.colors;                                   // the tubes

~pad = \orange.brush("Cm7 Fm9 Abmaj7 G7", 4);   ~pad.play;
~pad = \orange.brush("Cm7 Fm9 Abmaj7 G7", 4).darker(0.3);   // the same stroke, darker
~pad.cooler;                                    // move the running proxy's pattern toward blue
~pad.paint(\violet);                            // or recolour it outright

~m  = \blue.mark("0 3 5 7", 0.25);  ~m.play;    // discrete events
~t  = \red.dab("x..x", 0.5);        ~t.play;    // touches on one note
~dr = \violet.drip(2);              ~dr.play;   // sparse, random touches

~r = { 55 };
~bed   = \grey.wash(~r);                ~bed.fade(8).play;    // a bed at the root
~cloud = \cyan.spray(~r, dens: 25);     ~cloud.fade(4).play;  // a cloud at the root
~bed   = \grey.mix(\blue, 0.4).wash(~r);                      // a pigment between two tubes

// drop the register: a stroke is a Pbind like any other
~m = \blue.mark("0 3 5 7", 0.25).fast(2).jux(_.slow(2));
~m = Pbindf(\blue.mark("0 3 5 7", 0.25), \hue, Pseq([0.1, 0.6], inf));

// a drone recipe that names the axes joins the register
Synesthesia.droneRecipes[\lit] = { |root, mult = 1, wob = 0.1, amp = 0.3|
	var f = root * mult;
	RLPF.ar(Saw.ar([f, f * 1.003], 0.2), f * \val.kr(0.5).linexp(0, 1, 1, 24), 0.3) * \amp.kr(amp)
};
~a = \lit.drone(~r);  ~a.play;
~a.darker(0.2);                                 // moves the \val control
::
